  "notes": "Terre Haute pressing of the first-state gatefold jacket back cover with no violin credit on B4, and Jon Landau's producer credit misspelled as \"John Landau,\" covered by a corrective sticker over the producer credits.\n\n\"T\" etched in runouts denotes [l=Columbia Records Pressing Plant, Terre Haute], pressing. Remainder of runouts etched, plating letters stamped.\n\nA Terre Haute pressing version with updated credits on back cover also exists, at [r=1874253].\n\nIssued in a gatefold jacket with lyrics and credits.\n\nRecorded, mixed, and mastered at Record Plant Studio, New York, N.Y.\nB1: Recorded at 914 Sound Studio, Blauvelt, N.Y.\n\n[a=Randy Brecker] and [a=Michael Brecker]: Appear courtesy of [l=Arista Records].\n[a=David Sancious]: Appears courtesy of [l=Epic Records].\nDave Sanborn: Appears courtesy of [l=Warner Reprise].\n\nAll selections © 1975 Laurel Canyon Music Ltd. (ASCAP) except B1, © 1974 Laurel Canyon Music Ltd. (ASCAP).\n\n© 1975 CBS Inc. / ℗ 1975 CBS Inc. / Manufactured by Columbia Records / CBS Inc.",
